  "label": "User projected onto the textual message accusing Google of controlling information",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material (text_chunk_1) which uses second-person pronouns ('your family', 'you'll know') to directly address the viewer, making them the subject of the accusation. The user is implicitly positioned as the one whose perception is being manipulated and whose action (standing en masse) is being called for. This creates a direct semiotic projection where the viewer is made to feel personally implicated in the scenario described.",
